---
import Plate from '../../plate/Plate.astro';
import { renderFormula } from '../../../lib/formulas/render';
import { E, U0, numericalRangeBoundary, topSingularPairReal, confocalPoint, type Point } from './math';
import { CUES, FILM_DURATION, formatTime } from './story';
import './factor-two.css';

const formula = (tex: string) => renderFormula(tex, false);

const escape = (text: string) => text.replaceAll('&', '&amp;').replaceAll('<', '&lt;').replaceAll('>', '&gt;');

function subtitle(text: string): string {
  const pieces: string[] = [];
  let position = 0;

  for (const match of text.matchAll(/\$([^$\n]+)\$/g)) {
    pieces.push(escape(text.slice(position, match.index)));
    pieces.push(`<span class="ftfilm-phrase">${formula(match[1] ?? '')}</span>`);
    position = match.index + match[0].length;
  }

  pieces.push(escape(text.slice(position)));

  return pieces.join('');
}

const labels = [
  { id: 'matrix-d', tex: String.raw`D=\begin{pmatrix}1.5&0\\0&0.6\end{pmatrix}`, matrix: true, wide: false },
  { id: 'matrix-a', tex: String.raw`A=\begin{pmatrix}0&2\\0&0\end{pmatrix}`, matrix: true, wide: false },
  { id: 'matrix-e', tex: String.raw`E=\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\0&-1\end{pmatrix}`, matrix: true, wide: false },
  { id: 'scalar-bound', tex: String.raw`\|p(A)\|\le2\max_{z\in W(A)}|p(z)|`, matrix: false, wide: true },
  { id: 'complete-evaluation', tex: String.raw`P[A]=\sum_kA^k\otimes B_k`, matrix: false, wide: true },
  { id: 'noncommuting', tex: String.raw`B_1B_2\ne B_2B_1`, matrix: false, wide: false },
  { id: 'paulsen', tex: String.raw`S=\operatorname{diag}(1,2)`, matrix: false, wide: false },
  { id: 'constant-2017', tex: String.raw`1+\sqrt2`, matrix: false, wide: false },
  { id: 'quadratic', tex: String.raw`x^{*}Ax`, matrix: false, wide: false },
  { id: 'sweep-vector', tex: String.raw`x=(\cos\theta,\ e^{i\varphi}\sin\theta)`, matrix: false, wide: true },
  { id: 'range', tex: String.raw`W(A)`, matrix: false, wide: false },
  { id: 'ellipse-range', tex: String.raw`W(E)`, matrix: false, wide: false },
  { id: 'h-map', tex: String.raw`h(\lambda)=a\lambda+b/\lambda`, matrix: false, wide: true },
  { id: 'positivity', tex: String.raw`R+R^{*}\succeq0`, matrix: false, wide: false },
];

function outline(points: readonly Point[], centreX: number, centreY: number, scale: number): string {
  return points.map((point, index) => `${index === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'}${centreX + point.x * scale} ${centreY - point.y * scale}`).join('') + 'Z';
}

const boundary = numericalRangeBoundary(E, 240);
const domain = Array.from({ length: 240 }, (_, index) => confocalPoint(U0, index / 240 * Math.PI * 2));
const pair = topSingularPairReal(E);
const image = { x: pair.output.x * pair.norm, y: pair.output.y * pair.norm };
const factorX = (value: number) => 104 + (value - 1.8) / .8 * 204;
---

<Plate
  caption="A matrix whose eigenvalues are zero doubles a length, and the region swept out by x*Ax sees it: the factor two, its history from 11.08, and the claimed complete version, with the direct proof's positivity drawn on a 2 × 2 example."
  leftOut="the Faber-type polynomials and coefficient estimate; the three functionals and their dual norms; the resolvent's coefficient arrays; the structural route's minimizing metric, extremal vectors and density systems; the density Λ and representation formula; holomorphic and rational functions; the passage to bounded operators; degenerate ranges; Delyon and Delyon; applications in GMRES and rational Krylov methods; Lean. The FG/GF step is schematic."
>
  <uruk-factor-two>
    <div class="ftfilm">
      <div class="ftfilm-stage" data-film-viewport>
        <canvas class="ftfilm-canvas" data-film-canvas role="img" aria-label="A film showing how matrices stretch vectors, how their numerical ranges record more than their eigenvalues, and why the factor two is sharp. Separate scalar and complete lanes distinguish the checked scalar theorem from OpenAI's unreviewed complete claim. A complete text transcript follows."></canvas>
        <div class="ftfilm-still" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="ftfilm-still-plane">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 320 250" role="presentation">
              <text x="160" y="16" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="14">THE NUMERICAL RANGE OF E</text>
              <line x1="34" y1="115" x2="286" y2="115" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".6" />
              <line x1="160" y1="27" x2="160" y2="205" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".6" />
              <text x="290" y="119" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="13">real</text>
              <text x="166" y="37" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="13">imaginary</text>
              <path d={outline(boundary, 160, 115, 62)} fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.2" />
              <path d={outline(domain, 160, 115, 62)} fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-dasharray="2 4" />
              {[-1, 1].map((value) => <><circle cx={160 + value * 62} cy="115" r="3.4" fill="var(--ink)" /><text x={160 + value * 62} y="134" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="14">{value}</text></>)}
              <text x="160" y="191" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="12">Ω SHRUNK TO W(E)</text>
              <circle cx="51" cy="215" r="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width=".8" />
              <circle cx="51" cy="215" r="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="1 2" />
              <text x="180" y="216" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="15">R + R* ≥ 0 · minimum 0</text>
              <text x="160" y="245" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="11">2 × 2 EXAMPLE · KNOWN SINCE 2006</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="ftfilm-still-stretch">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 360 180" role="presentation">
              <text x="180" y="16" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="14">THE LARGEST STRETCH</text>
              <circle cx="77" cy="92" r="30" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".7" />
              <line x1="11" y1="92" x2="158" y2="92" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".5" />
              <line x1="77" y1="31" x2="77" y2="143" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".5" />
              <line x1="77" y1="92" x2={77 + pair.input.x * 30} y2={92 - pair.input.y * 30} stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1" />
              <circle cx={77 + pair.input.x * 30} cy={92 - pair.input.y * 30} r="2" fill="var(--ink)" />
              <line x1="77" y1="92" x2={77 + image.x * 30} y2={92 - image.y * 30} stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.7" />
              <circle cx={77 + image.x * 30} cy={92 - image.y * 30} r="2.6" fill="var(--ink)" />
              <text x="255" y="49" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-garamond-math)" font-size="22">E = [ 1  2 ; 0  −1 ]</text>
              <text x="255" y="77" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="13">‖E‖ = {pair.norm.toFixed(3)}</text>
              <rect x="197" y="96" width={pair.norm * 35} height="9" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" />
              <rect x="197" y="126" width={2 * Math.SQRT2 * 35} height="9" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" />
              <text x="255" y="121" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="13">2 × √2 = 2.828</text>
              <text x="180" y="165" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="13">p(z) = z · BELOW, WITH ROOM</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="ftfilm-still-scale">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 360 127" role="presentation">
              <text x="180" y="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="13">THE FACTOR, FOR EVERY MATRIX</text>
              {[48, 82].map((y) => <line x1="104" y1={y} x2="308" y2={y} stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".7" />)}
              <text x="13" y="52" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="13">SCALAR</text>
              <text x="13" y="86" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="13">COMPLETE</text>
              <line x1={factorX(2)} y1="39" x2={factorX(2)} y2="57" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.8" />
              <line x1={factorX(2)} y1="72" x2={factorX(2)} y2="92" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-dasharray="3 2" />
              <text x={factorX(2) + 15} y="42" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="12">2 · CHECKED</text>
              <text x={factorX(2) + 15} y="100" fill="var(--blue)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="12">2 · UNREVIEWED</text>
              <text x="180" y="124" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="12">The scalar check is a different theorem.</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ftfilm-formulas" aria-hidden="true" data-bleed>
          {labels.map((label) => <span class:list={['ftfilm-label', { 'ftfilm-label--matrix': label.matrix, 'ftfilm-label--wide': label.wide }]} data-label={label.id}><span set:html={formula(label.tex)} /></span>)}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ftfilm-subtitles" aria-hidden="true">
        {CUES.map((cue, index) => <p class:list={['ftfilm-cue', { 'is-active': index === CUES.length - 1 }]} data-cue={index}><span set:html={subtitle(cue.text)} /><span class="ftfilm-citations"> {cue.sources.map((source) => `[${source}]`).join('')}</span></p>)}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ftfilm-controls" data-script-only>
      <div class="ftfilm-buttons">
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-play><span data-play-label>Pause</span></button>
        <p class="ftfilm-clock"><span data-film-clock>0:00 / {formatTime(FILM_DURATION)}</span></p>
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-film-restart>Restart</button>
      </div>
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="ftfilm-timeline">Film timeline. Arrow keys move one subtitle at a time.</label>
      <input id="ftfilm-timeline" class="ftfilm-timeline" data-film-range type="range" min="0" max={FILM_DURATION} step="100" value="0" />
      <div class="ftfilm-steps">
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-film-previous>Previous</button>
        <p>Step through without motion</p>
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-film-next>Next</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="visually-hidden" data-film-status aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
    <details class="ftfilm-transcript">
      <summary class="text-link">Read the film as text</summary>
      <ol>{CUES.map((cue) => <li><h3>{cue.title}</h3><p><span set:html={subtitle(cue.text)} /> {cue.sources.map((source) => <> <a class="citation text-link" href={`#source-${source}`}>[{source}]</a></>)}</p></li>)}</ol>
      <p class="ftfilm-method">How the film is made. Every numerical range is computed from its matrix. At each direction, the top eigenvector of the Hermitian part of the rotated matrix gives a boundary point. The real-vector ring and its image are computed separately; they illustrate matrix action, while the numerical range uses complex unit vectors. The opening matrix D is diagonal, with norm 1.5. Its linear morph into A first decreases the norm to about 1.223 before reaching 2, as the readout shows.</p>
      <p class="ftfilm-method">For A = [0, 2; 0, 0], both eigenvalues are zero, its norm is 2, and its numerical range is exactly the closed unit disk. The spiral uses the complex vector <span set:html={formula(String.raw`x=(\cos\theta,e^{i\varphi}\sin\theta)`)} />, whose numerical value is <span set:html={formula(String.raw`\sin2\theta\,e^{i\varphi}`)} />. It samples that disk; a finite trace illustrates the full sweep. With p(z) = z, the left side of the inequality is 2 and the maximum on the disk is 1. The swap-matrix coefficient gives the same sharp ratio for a matrix-valued polynomial. The noncommuting tiles are separate explicit examples of products whose order changes their value.</p>
      <p class="ftfilm-method">Paulsen's example changes the inner product using S = diag(1, 2). Its unit ball is |x₁|² + 4|x₂|² ≤ 1. The similarity SAS⁻¹ has norm 1, and the condition number of S is 2. This is computed for the displayed matrix; it illustrates the general equivalence stated in the article.</p>
      <p class="ftfilm-method">The second morph uses M(t) = [t, 2; 0, −t]. Its numerical range is an ellipse with semi-axes √(1 + t²) and 1, and its eigenvalues ±t are its foci. At t = 1 the matrix E has norm 1 + √2, numerical radius √2, and E² = I. The coincidence of its norm with the 2017 universal constant does not identify those two quantities. For p(z) = z, the two bars read about 2.414 and 2.828.</p>
      <p class="ftfilm-method">For the proof picture, Ω is a confocal ellipse with semi-axes cosh u and sinh u. The exact exterior map is h(λ) = aλ + b/λ, where a = eᵘ/2 and b = e⁻ᵘ/2. The band computes the least eigenvalue of R + R*, with R(λ) = λh′(λ)(h(λ)I − E)⁻¹, at each point of the unit circle. It stays positive while Ω strictly contains W(E), and touches zero at u = asinh 1, where the two boundaries meet. The shrinking stops there. A hairline remains when the band has zero thickness.</p>
      <p class="ftfilm-method">The FG/GF tiles and the general proof's functionals are schematic. The numerical ranges, singular vectors, norms, balance values and boundary band are computed on exact 2 × 2 examples. That case was known in 2006. The claimed new content concerns every matrix size, every coefficient size, and bounded operators; these finite drawings do not verify it. The two history lanes use published constants, with a solid scalar mark and a dashed blue complete claim. The article's review of the scalar theorem does not cover the complete papers.</p>
    </details>
  </uruk-factor-two>
</Plate>

<script>
  import './element';
</script>
